---
/**
 * HifOxygenSwitch — HIF-1α is made all the time and destroyed all the time; the oxygen-dependent
 * mark is what lets the destruction happen. One oxygen slider (low to normal), a choice of whether
 * VHL works, and a time slider (minutes since the change). Output: a tank for the HIF-1α level
 * (relative to the level in normal oxygen) and a lamp for its target genes.
 * Lesson facts only: half-life of about five minutes in normal oxygen, destruction stops when
 * hydroxylation stops, pool about five times baseline after 30 minutes. Everything else is
 * labelled "in this sketch". Original.
 */
---

<figure class="hx card" data-hifswitch>
  <figcaption class="hx-head">HIF-1α — oxygen writes the destruction mark<span class="hx-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <div class="hx-steps" aria-label="The four steps that destroy HIF-1α">
    <div class="hx-step" data-step="mark"><b>1 · Mark</b><span>Oxygen-dependent hydroxyl on a proline of HIF-1α</span><em data-st="mark"></em></div>
    <div class="hx-step" data-step="vhl"><b>2 · VHL reads</b><span>VHL grips the hydroxylated proline</span><em data-st="vhl"></em></div>
    <div class="hx-step" data-step="chain"><b>3 · Ubiquitin chain</b><span>The cullin-RING ligase builds a chain</span><em data-st="chain"></em></div>
    <div class="hx-step" data-step="prot"><b>4 · Proteasome</b><span>HIF-1α is destroyed</span><em data-st="prot"></em></div>
  </div>

  <svg class="hx-svg" viewBox="0 0 340 190" role="img" aria-label="A tank showing the amount of HIF-1 alpha relative to its level in normal oxygen, and a lamp showing whether its target genes are on" data-svg>
    <text x="8" y="14" font-size="10" fill="#4b4b55">HIF-1α amount (relative units)</text>
    <rect x="40" y="22" width="90" height="140" fill="#fff" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <rect x="41" y="161" width="88" height="0" fill="#0e7c86" data-fill/>
    <line x1="34" y1="140" x2="136" y2="140" stroke="#e57200" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" data-base/>
    <text x="140" y="143" font-size="9" fill="#b34f00" data-baselabel>level in normal oxygen = 1</text>
    <text x="36" y="26" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" text-anchor="end">6</text>
    <text x="36" y="165" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" text-anchor="end">0</text>
    <text x="85" y="180" font-size="10" fill="#4b4b55" text-anchor="middle" data-val>1.0 ×</text>
    <circle cx="270" cy="60" r="22" fill="#e8e8ee" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1.2" data-lamp/>
    <text x="270" y="64" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#2a2a33" data-lamptext>OFF</text>
    <text x="270" y="100" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#4b4b55">target genes</text>
    <text x="270" y="113" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" fill="#4b4b55">(e.g. erythropoietin, VEGF)</text>
    <text x="270" y="130" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" fill="#4b4b55">once HIF-1α pairs with ARNT</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="hx-controls">
    <label class="hx-slabel"><span>Oxygen: <em data-out="o2">normal</em> <small>(low ← → normal)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="o2" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="100" />
    </label>
    <label class="hx-slabel"><span>Minutes since the change: <em data-out="t">30</em></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="t" min="0" max="30" step="1" value="30" />
    </label>
    <fieldset class="hx-fs"><legend>Which part is broken?</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="hx-part" value="none" checked /> None, all parts work</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="hx-part" value="vhl" /> VHL lost</label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>

  <p class="hx-why" data-why role="status"></p>

  <p class="hx-foot">Keep the rule: HIF-1α is made all the time and destroyed all the time, so stopping the destruction, with low oxygen or with no VHL, raises it without any new transcription. In this sketch the level is relative to normal oxygen, the half-life of about five minutes applies only to normal oxygen, the destruction rate is taken as proportional to the oxygen level, and "on" means more than twice the normal level. The picture is a sketch of the logic, not a measurement. The lamp reads ON above 2 × normal, and destruction is set in proportion to oxygen: both are this sketch's choices. Where a slider changes nothing, the logic says nothing changes.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-hifswitch]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends Element>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const o2In = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="o2"]'), tIn = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="t"]');
    const o2Out = q<HTMLElement>('[data-out="o2"]'), tOut = q<HTMLElement>('[data-out="t"]');
    const why = q<HTMLElement>('[data-why]');
    const fill = q<SVGRectElement>('[data-fill]'), val = q<SVGTextElement>('[data-val]');
    const lamp = q<SVGCircleElement>('[data-lamp]'), lampText = q<SVGTextElement>('[data-lamptext]');
    const radios = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="hx-part"]'));
    const K = Math.LN2 / 5; // per minute: half-life of about five minutes in normal oxygen (lesson)
    const MAXV = 6, TOP = 22, BOT = 162, TH = BOT - TOP;
    const setStep = (key: string, cls: string, text: string) => {
      q<HTMLElement>(`[data-step="${key}"]`).className = 'hx-step hx-' + cls;
      q<HTMLElement>(`[data-st="${key}"]`).textContent = text;
    };
    function render() {
      const O = parseInt(o2In.value, 10) / 100, t = parseInt(tIn.value, 10);
      const vhlLost = radios.find((r) => r.checked)!.value === 'vhl';
      o2Out.textContent = O >= 1 ? 'normal' : O <= 0 ? 'low' : Math.round(O * 100) + '% of normal';
      tOut.textContent = String(t);
      // mark written in proportion to oxygen (sketch); destruction needs the mark AND VHL
      const ke = vhlLost ? 0 : K * O;
      const lvl = ke === 0 ? 1 + K * t : (K / ke) * (1 - Math.exp(-ke * t)) + Math.exp(-ke * t);
      const shown = Math.min(lvl, MAXV);
      const h = (shown / MAXV) * TH;
      fill.setAttribute('y', String(BOT - h)); fill.setAttribute('height', String(h));
      val.textContent = lvl.toFixed(1) + ' × the level in normal oxygen';
      const baseY = BOT - (1 / MAXV) * TH;
      q('[data-base]').setAttribute('y1', String(baseY)); q('[data-base]').setAttribute('y2', String(baseY));
      q('[data-baselabel]').setAttribute('y', String(baseY + 3));
      const on = lvl > 2;
      lamp.setAttribute('fill', on ? '#f6c344' : '#e8e8ee'); lampText.textContent = on ? 'ON' : 'OFF';

      // step states (text carries the meaning, colour only helps)
      const markTxt = O >= 1 ? 'written' : O <= 0 ? 'not written' : 'written less often';
      setStep('mark', O >= 1 ? 'on' : O <= 0 ? 'off' : 'part', markTxt);
      if (vhlLost) {
        setStep('vhl', 'off', 'VHL lost: mark not read');
        setStep('chain', 'off', 'no chain built');
        setStep('prot', 'off', 'not sent');
      } else {
        const s = O >= 1 ? 'on' : O <= 0 ? 'off' : 'part';
        setStep('vhl', s, O >= 1 ? 'reads the mark' : O <= 0 ? 'nothing to grip' : 'less to grip');
        setStep('chain', s, O >= 1 ? 'built' : O <= 0 ? 'not built' : 'built less often');
        setStep('prot', s, O >= 1 ? 'destroyed' : O <= 0 ? 'spared' : 'destroyed less often');
      }

      const x = lvl.toFixed(1);
      let msg: string;
      if (vhlLost) {
        const markNote = O >= 1 ? 'The prolyl hydroxylase still writes the mark in air, but VHL is the part that reads it' : O <= 0 ? 'With little oxygen the mark is not even written, and VHL is gone as well' : 'The mark is written only partly, and VHL, the part that reads it, is gone';
        msg = `${markNote}, so no ubiquitin chain is built and nothing sends HIF-1α to the proteasome. It builds up whatever the oxygen. ` +
          (t === 0 ? 'At the moment of the change the level is still the normal one.' : `In this sketch it is ${x} × normal after ${t} minutes, and the target genes are ${on ? 'on' : 'not on'}.`);
      } else if (O >= 1) {
        msg = `Oxygen is plentiful, so the prolyl hydroxylase hydroxylates a proline, VHL grips it, a chain is built and the proteasome destroys HIF-1α, with a half-life of about five minutes. The level stays at its normal low value and the target genes stay off.`;
      } else {
        const how = O <= 0 ? 'Oxygen is low, so the hydroxylation is not finished, VHL has nothing to grip and destruction stops' : 'Oxygen is lower, so the enzyme finishes the reaction less often, fewer prolines are hydroxylated, VHL has less to grip and HIF-1α is spared more';
        msg = `${how}. HIF-1α is still being made, so it builds up with no new transcription. ` +
          (t === 0 ? 'At the moment of the change the level is still the normal one.' : `In this sketch it is ${x} × normal after ${t} minutes, and the target genes are ${on ? 'on, because HIF-1α can pair with ARNT in the nucleus' : 'not yet on'}.`);
      }
      why.textContent = msg;
    }
    [o2In, tIn, ...radios].forEach((c) => c.addEventListener('input', render));
    render();
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .hx { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .hx-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .hx-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .hx-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(130px, 1fr)); gap: var(--ddp-space-2); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .hx-step { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.15rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; border: 2px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; background: #fff; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .hx-step b { color: var(--ddp-color-primary); }
  .hx-step em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); }
  .hx-step.hx-on { border-color: #0e7c86; background: #e6f4f5; }
  .hx-step.hx-part { border-color: #e57200; border-style: dashed; background: #fff4e8; }
  .hx-step.hx-off { border-color: #8a8a94; border-style: dotted; background: #f0f0f3; }
  .hx-svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; height: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .hx-controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 var(--ddp-space-2); }
  .hx-slabel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .hx-slabel small { font-size: inherit; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .hx-slabel em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-accent); font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); }
  .hx-slabel input { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); }
  .hx-fs { grid-column: 1 / -1; border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.3rem 1rem; }
  .hx-fs legend { padding: 0 0.3rem; }
  .hx-why { margin: 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; min-height: 4.5em; }
  .hx-foot { margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--ddp-color-secondary); padding-left: 0.55rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .hx-controls { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
